 seventh we have a spell so  epic that it gave me goosebumps the  first time I saw it like actual  goosebumps the sea dragons role was  first used by Noel to disarm vetto  and yeah I do mean that literally even  though she's royalty Noel has always  struggled to control her magic ever  since a young age this seeming lack of  innate skill was enough to have her  verbally abused by her family pretty  much her whole life and I cannot tell  you how much I wanted to slap this guy  now the whole underwater temple hug that  was amazing for Noel's development and  she was the only one who could actually  transport everyone to the underwater  temple and then when in the temple she  discovered for the first time that she  has an attack spell the sea dragons roar  was a one-shot spell for many  reasons I mean Vito is a member of the  third eye which by default makes him one  of these strongest characters we've ever  seen and by this point he'd effortlessly  resisted attacks from LARC magna and the  sea temple guy so the fact that Noel was  able to break through his defensive  magic rip off his arm and then crash  through the walls of the sea temple like  this was certainly a spell that could  wash off someone if used accurately  firing into sixth place we have one of  juego leon spells and i'm gonna be  upfront here guys there's a lot of bias  involved here because for girly on to me  is the coolest magic night captain there  is like period his Flame magic was on  full display during the attack on the  world capital and he used it to  incinerate several powerful puppets  being controlled by wraiths magic many  of the spells he displayed could be  classified as one-shot including this  one here which is just visually amazing  but I want to turn your attention to the  sole linear attack of which the japanese  translation literally means sun beam of  the miniature sun why is this guy so  cool this ball delivers a concentrated  beam of fire and it pierced through the  barrier of a resurrected corpse and this  was interesting because this corpse used  to be a defense magic expert and it had  been brought back from the dead and then  had its barrier in hearts by curse magic  so although for Guerlain skill was a big  factor in being able to pierce this  barrier no one could deny that being  able to break through this in any  scenario you have to be pretty  overpowered the sole linea attack was  enough to incinerate this corpse after  only making one hit and in anime we see  it used to destroy a horde of zombies in  one strike so yeah not much more to it  than that  definitely one of the best one shots we  saw this season at fifth place we have a  pretty interesting one and it has some  notable differences from the rest of  this list  so rather than instantly piercing or  dismembering the opponent in some way  this spell absorbs their magic and then  grows a tree around their body and we  saw the captain of the Golden Dawn use  this to kill one of these shining  generals of the diamond Kingdom yeah the  diamond kingdom has taken some massive  elves in this series now mistltein seed  is an awesome one-shot spell that  requires minimal effort from the user  like if we do a slow-motion replay right  here all he did was casually throw this  seed he didn't even put his back into it  and as if that wasn't enough because the  spell seemingly converts the person into  a tree in some way by using their magic  I I have to say this is probably one of  the most eco-friendly attacks we've ever  seen personally I found tree magic to be  really creative and intriguing  and I gotta give credit to the manga  curve being so creative because if you  had told me about the idea of offensive  tree magic I would have assumed that it  either be really weak or pretty  worthless not that I have anything  against trees but it's not like  something like fire or electricity where  you can clearly see how it could be  harmful but the way that William  Vengeance has used this so far from what  I've seen it's got me thinking that tree  magic is actually very very useful  moving on to fourth we have a few spells  from Licht who is clearly the  overarching antagonist of season one and  beyond Lakes possesses powerful light  magic that among other things allows him  to teleport at light speed at least I  assume this is light speed if not I'm  gonna be really disappointed when we  first probably get a look at him he uses  these darts made of light to stab a stir  in the leg and basically just destroy  this sister he was hitting everyone with  these things and I'm sure in the right  circumstances if it hit like a vital  organ this could be a one-shot spell but  I have to say that everyone I just  mentioned who got hit by these things  did survive however his finishing move  this spell was acknowledged as too fast  for Yami or asked her to evade do you  know how strong a spell has to be for  Yami to not bother to try and fight back  just think about that so in this  situation to use the spell he charged up  the light between his hands for a period  of time and then released this massive  concentrated beam of light good thing  that gauche was able to show up and  reflect it but I think we can already  notice that had he not done that both  the army and asked her would have been  disintegrated by this thing and it's  probably worth noting that he did have  another one-shot spell in season one but  we didn't actually get to see its full  capability because he was sealed away so  he couldn't really use it and so I don't  really count it on this list but I do  acknowledge that for magic night captain  seemingly believed that they would not  be able to stop it  moving into the top three the bronze  medal goes to our very special boy and  this bit of spirit magic which we first  saw used in the dungeon exploration arc  so in this moment aster was about to be  one shot hit by Mars after already  suffering a pretty serious injury anyone  who could have saved him was either  trapped inside a crystal or just unable  to do so but you know in typical you  know fashion manages to bust out of the  crystal and then out of nowhere it looks  like time is frozen this is of course  where we meet SIL for the first time and  she casually blow some air which then  shatters this massive crystal sword and  Mars his crystal armor in the process  from what I've seen spirit magic is just  like on a different  to everything else cuz to be able to  shutter this giant thing with a single  breath I can only imagine what happens  when she sneezes we see them use this  attack again during you nose battle with  this witch and while it didn't exactly  one shot hers and kill her she did have  to use up all of her magic to survive  the attack which turned up from looking  like this to looking like this so uh  overall I have no regret in saying that  this spell can do a lot of damage and is  definitely capable of being a one-shot  attack at second place we have a spell  possessed by the wizard king himself who  only showed off his powers once during  season one and I think this moment was  quite similar to when Miriah whipped the  entirety of class 1a because Julius  appears out of nowhere right and then he  instantly wastes a couple of I of the  Midnight Sun members now the wizard King  uses time magic which is clearly as epic  as it sounds and this particular spell  wasn't given a name from what I could  remember but when I watched this like I  can't remember if I laughed or gasped  probably a combination of both to be  honest because it was so absurd and just  like out of the blue because we hadn't  seen his power or magic at this point so  yeah it was really shocking moment but  pretty funny as well there's a part of  this whole scene that we didn't see in  the anime but when I read back the manga  I did actually notice when Licht appears  the manga shows us that Julius creates  another one of these time bulls which is  obviously how Licht ended up with his  disfigured arm which we did see in the  anime but we didn't see how it went down  or what spell Julius used so yeah I mean  this whatever this is called amazing  I assume the way it works is that he  liked fast forwards their lifespan until  they're like just nothing and now after  a lot of talk let's get into the best  one-shot spell in season 1 of black  clover as I'm sure you all remember  during the underwater temple arc vetto  was about to self-destruct and just blow  the place up having been thoroughly  beaten by the teamwork of the black  balls but the entire time Yami was  unavailable due to being trapped by this  spatial magic user so once he did  eventually escape he pushed past his  limits and learnt this new one shot  spell which has an amazing name so this  is the dark cloaked dimension slash and  honestly it was just absurd so this was  able to cut straight through vetto like  it sliced him right down the middle and  remember that licked even said the  members of the third eye their strength  surpasses even his own but as Yami said  it doesn't matter how strong the person  receiving this spell is because you're  getting one shotted through the  dimensions like look at the line this  left in the ground here honestly it's so  cool  I'm sure if you're this far into the  video you already know this but Yami  uses dark magic and this right here was  one of the many examples that just  validated his insane strength  on a sidenote is pretty surprising to me  that Yami is only 28 like you can't tell  me he doesn't have powerful middle-aged  energy with that said those are the  eight best one-shot spells in season 1  of black clover in my opinion there are  many others to choose from but these  ones right here stood out to me  especially let me know any that you  think might deserve a place on this list  and do let me know in the comments if  you want me to do more black clover  content I was initially planning to get  fully up to date with